  ??1CommandReturnObject@lldb_private@@QEAA@XZ
; ??1DumpValueObjectOptions@lldb_private@@QEAA@XZ
;   Deliberately not exported. Unlike the other destructors here,
;   DumpValueObjectOptions declares none, so the implicit one is inline and
;   -O2 elides it rather than emitting a standalone symbol. Naming it here
;   makes it a link root, and the DLL then fails to link with
;   "lld-link: error: <root>: undefined symbol" under --compilation_mode=opt,
;   which is the mode README.md recommends. It links under dbg only because
;   -O0 emits the inline copy.
;
;   Nothing needs the export: no undefined reference to it exists in any of
;   the 112 lldb libraries or in KGEN/lib/MojoLLDB. A consumer that destroys
;   one has the full class definition from DumpValueObjectOptions.h and emits
;   its own inline destructor. The copy constructor above stays exported
;   because that one is genuinely out of line.
  ??1FileSpec@lldb_private@@QEAA@XZ
